  {
   "urn": "urn:mavedb:00001258-a-1",
   "title": "Selection of loss-of-function SPOP via yeast survival assay",
   "shortDescription": "An amino acid level deep mutational scan of human SPOP using yeast survival assay.",
   "publishedDate": "2025-12-24",
   "replacesId": null,
   "numVariants": 7441,
   "experiment": {
    "title": "SPOP yeast growth inhibition",
    "shortDescription": "Deep Mutational Scan of the human SPOP using yeast growth inhibition reveals comprehensive functional landscape of variants.",
    "abstractText": "To comprehensively characterize the functional landscape of SPOP alteration, we performed a deep mutational screening (DMS), elucidating the functionality of 7,933 out of 8,228 possible single amino acid changes (96.4% coverage). Leveraging the observation that overexpression of human SPOP leads to yeast growth arrest, we assessed the functionality of each variant using a yeast proliferation assay.",
    "methodText": "DMS library was synthesized through tile-based cloning. We observed that expression of wild-type SPOP inhibits yeast growth, whereas depletion of specific functional regions within wild-type SPOP, namely the MATH, BTB, and 3-box domains, rescues it. To take advantage of the complementary strengths of both platforms, we analyze our mutant libraries using short-read and long-read sequencing.",
